1
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
At last! Alvin's first motion picture.

2
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:14,000
The Chipmunk Adventure is a animation, family,
adventure film directed by Janice Karman.

3
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:48,000
The Chipmunks and the Chipettes go head to head in a hot air
balloon race, and the winner gets $100,000.

4
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Unbeknownst to the participants, the "race" is
actually a diamond smuggling ring!

5
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:56,000
David Seville / Alvin Seville / Simon Seville
(voice), played by Ross Bagdasarian, Jr..

6
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Theodore / Brittany / Jeanette / Eleanor (voice), played by Janice Karman.

7
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Miss Rebecca Miller (voice), played by Dody Goodman.

8
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Claudia Furschtien (voice), played by Susan Tyrrell.

9
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Klaus Furschtien (voice), played by Anthony De Longis.

10
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Sophie / Native Chief / Baby Penguin / Additional
Voices (voice), played by Frank Welker.

11
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:20,000
The Chipmunk Adventure is a 1987 American animated musical–adventure comedy film based on the Saturday-morning cartoon series Alvin
and the Chipmunks and the Alvin and the Chipmunks virtual band and media franchise created by Ross Bagdasarian Sr.

12
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
The film was directed by Janice Karman and written
by Karman and Ross Bagdasarian Jr.

13
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:28,000
As the events of the film take place between the fourth and fifth seasons of Alvin and the Chipmunks, the plot follows the Chipmunks and the Chipettes as they go on a
hot air balloon race around the world while their guardian David Seville is out on a trip, not knowing that it is a cover for a diamond smuggling ring.

14
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:02,000
The chipmunks travel through a series of adventures in different countries while being
hunted down by the diamond smugglers, Claudia and Klaus Furschtein.

15
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
After the success of the Alvin and the Chipmunks television series on NBC, several
companies had been interested in financing an Alvin and the Chipmunks film.

16
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Bagdasarian Jr.

17
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:44,000
and Karman decided to finance the movie themselves.

18
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Animators from The Black Cauldron (1985) worked on the film after its box-office
flop caused many animators to get laid off from Walt Disney Pictures.

19
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:52,000
The animation was provided overseas to several regions such as Utah and Canada.

20
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Randy Edelman composed the music after he was visited by Bagdasarian Jr.

21
00:53:54,000 --> 00:54:00,000
Production of the film lasted for a year to be completed.

22
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:34,000
The Chipmunk Adventure was released on May 22, 1987, and grossed $6.8 million
at the box office, making it a moderate box-office success.

23
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:08,000
The film initially received mixed reviews from critics.

24
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Most critics praised the animation, visuals, and soundtrack, but the plot
and voices of the Chipmunks and Chipettes were polarizing.

25
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
The film's reliance on racial stereotyping was also criticized.

26
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:50,000
Retrospective reviews of the film became more positive.

27
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
It was the Chipmunks' first theatrical film; the franchise's second film,
Alvin and the Chipmunks, was released on December 14, 2007.

28
01:11:52,000 --> 01:11:58,000
The film explores themes of sibling relationship, single parent,
rome, italy, journey around the world, arabian.

29
01:14:26,000 --> 01:14:32,000
The tone is lighthearted.
